Template: qeli/run-as
Type: select
Choices: qeli, root
Default: qeli
Description: Run the qeli service as which user?
 The qeli VPN server can run as the unprivileged "qeli" system user
 (recommended: least privilege, the default hardened setup) or as "root".
 .
 Running as root removes the privilege separation: a compromise of the daemon
 becomes a compromise of the whole host. Pick it only when the qeli user cannot
 work (for example a kernel or container without ambient capabilities), or to
 avoid the /etc/qeli ownership and polkit setup. When unsure, keep "qeli".
 .
 You can change this at any time with:  qeli set-service-user root|qeli
